course: dictionary
lesson: 7737
title: Church words: pulpit
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A pulpit is a raised stand in a church. The priest or minister stands up there to give the sermon, which is a talk about the Bible and faith. Most pulpits are enclosed, so the speaker is set a little apart from the people in the pews.
explain: Look at the words around it to work out what it means. «The font for baptism, the pulpit for preaching, the lectern for reading» lists church parts and their jobs. The pattern "the X for Y" tells you a pulpit is for preaching.
explain: The word can also mean preachers or religious teaching in general. «He spoke from the pulpit» can mean he spoke as a preacher, not just that he stood in one place. Ask yourself: is the sentence about a place, or about the teaching? The clues will tell you which.
fact: A pulpit is a raised, enclosed stand in a church.
fact: The priest or minister gives the sermon from the pulpit.
fact: «The font, a big stone bowl for water often near the door, is used for baptism.»
fact: Other church parts include the altar, the lectern, the pews and the font.
fact: Pulpit can also mean preaching or religious teaching in general, as in «from the pulpit».
exercise: What is a pulpit? | A window with pictures of Bible stories | A stone bowl of water by the door | *A raised, enclosed stand in a church where the sermon is given | A long wooden bench where people sit
exercise: Ben reads, «The minister climbed into the pulpit.» Where is the minister now? | Sitting in the front pew | *Up in the raised stand where the sermon is given | Standing outside the church door | Kneeling at the font
exercise: «The font, a big stone bowl for water, is used for baptism.» Which church part is used for baptism? | The lectern | The pews | The altar | *The font
test: «He spoke from the pulpit about kindness.» In this sentence, what does pulpit most likely mean? | *Religious teaching or preaching | A stained-glass window | A church pew | A tall wooden desk for books
test: Which of these is NOT a church part from this lesson? | Lectern | Font | *Fountain | Altar
exam: What does «a bully pulpit» mean, a phrase used in the USA? | A bully who shouts in church | *A strong position from which to speak | A quiet corner of a church | A stand for books
